    <h3 class="dept-services-heading">The Green ICU Concept</h3>
    <p>Our ICU is designed around the "Green ICU" principle — a critical care environment engineered to minimise hospital-acquired infections while supporting faster, calmer recovery. Every bed is served by HEPA-filtered positive-pressure air handling, dedicated isolation zones for immunocompromised and highly infectious patients, controlled visitor traffic, and continuous environmental monitoring. Natural light, noise control, and single-point nursing supervision are built into the unit's layout to reduce patient stress and delirium — both of which are known to slow recovery in critically ill patients. The result is an ICU that is not only clinically advanced, but also safer and more humane for patients and the families waiting beside them.</p>

    <h3 class="dept-services-heading">Comprehensive Critical Care Services</h3>
    <ol class="services-list">
      <li><strong>Invasive &amp; Non-Invasive Ventilation Support</strong> — Advanced mechanical ventilators for patients in respiratory failure, with continuous monitoring by critical care specialists and trained ICU nursing staff.</li>
      <li><strong>Hemodynamic Monitoring</strong> — Continuous, beat-to-beat monitoring of blood pressure, cardiac output, and oxygenation to detect deterioration early and guide real-time treatment decisions.</li>
      <li><strong>HEPA-Filtered Isolation Bays</strong> — Dedicated Green ICU isolation beds with filtered air handling to protect immunocompromised patients and contain infectious cases.</li>
      <li><strong>Sepsis &amp; Multi-Organ Dysfunction Management</strong> — Protocol-driven sepsis bundles, renal support, and coordinated multi-specialty management for patients with failing organ systems.</li>
      <li><strong>Post-Surgical High-Risk Recovery</strong> — Close-monitoring recovery beds for high-risk orthopedic, oncology, and general surgery patients who need intensive observation immediately after major procedures.</li>
      <li><strong>24/7 Intensivist &amp; Code Blue Response</strong> — On-site critical care physicians and a trained code-blue team available around the clock for immediate emergency life support.</li>
    </ol>

